{
  "slug": "blueberry-and-lemon-muffins",
  "title": "Blueberry and Lemon Muffins",
  "blurb": "Light, fruity muffins made with brown rice flour and fresh blueberries, with a hint of lemon zest.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat your oven to 180°C and line a 12-hole muffin tin with paper cases.",
    "In a large bowl, whisk together the brown rice flour, tapioca flour, baking powder and salt.",
    "In another bowl, beat the eggs with the sugar until pale, then whisk in the oil, milk, vanilla extract and the finely grated zest of the lemon.",
    "Pour the wet ingredients into the dry and fold gently until just combined, then fold in the blueberries.",
    "Divide the batter evenly among the muffin cases, filling each about three-quarters full.",
    "Bake for 38 to 40 minutes until golden and a skewer inserted into the centre comes out clean.",
    "Leave the muffins to cool in the tin for 5 minutes, then transfer to a wire rack."
  ],
